       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose looks like a possible error.\n\nAmlodipine's usual adult oral dose is 2.5 to 10 mg once daily, and 10 mg/day is the labeled maximum. 50 mg is five times that maximum. Excess amlodipine can cause marked hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema, and the effects last a long time.\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose before I enter it. For example:\n- **5 mg PO once daily**, the usual starting dose\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum\n- **50 mg PO once daily**, if you intend this dose deliberately\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter it with the patient details (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function, no allergies) in the order note. If the 50 mg dose is intentional, please tell me the reason so I can include it in the note."
      }
